% These singularities stem from the scaling relations $\lambda^{q_i}$ in \eqref{eq:hcoor}, which originate from the lattice vectors $v_i$ of the $1$-dimensional cones in the fan (see \eqref{eq:Geq}). A singularity occurs when such vectors span a cone that fails to generate the full lattice. To resolve this, additional $1$-cones must be introduced to subdivide the fan.

