\begin{abstract}
Let $G$ be a locally compact group, $L(G)$ be its group von Neumann algebra equipped with the Plancherel weight $\varphi_G$. In this paper, we consider the following two questions. (1) When is the restriction of $\varphi_G$ to the subalgebra generated by a closed subgroup $H$ semifinite? If so, is it equal (up to a constant) to $\varphi_H$? (2) When is $L(G)$ a factor?
We give a complete answer to (1), and when $G$ is second countable, totally disconnected and admits a sufficiently large non-unimodular part, we provide an answer to (2). 
\end{abstract}

