%     Now, we consider the case $\mu_G(U)=\infty$. By \cite[Theorem 12.2]{HewittRoss1MR551496}, it suffices to show that $f=0$ locally $\mu_G$-a.e. on $U$. Take any Borel subset $B \subseteq G$ such that $\mu_G(B) < \infty$. By the outer regularity of $\mu_G$, there exists an open set $V$ such that $B\subseteq V$ and $\mu_G(V)<\infty$. Then, $V\cap U$ is an open set with finite measure. Since $C_c(G)_{V\cap U} \subseteq C_c(G)_U$, it follows that $\mu_G(N\cap V \cap U)=0$ by the previous argument. Therefore, we conclude that $\mu_G(N \cap B) \le \mu_G(N\cap V \cap U) =0$, hence $f=0$ locally $\mu_G$-a.e. on $U$. 
