Now, we obtain the main theorem. 

\begin{theorem}\label{plweightmainthm}
    For a locally compact group $G$ and a closed subgroup $H$, the following conditions are equivalent.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(i)] $H$ is open.
        \item[(ii)] $\varphi_G|L(H)$ is semifinte.
        \item[(iii)] $\varphi_G|L(H)=C\cdot\varphi_H$ for some constant $C>0$.
     \end{enumerate}
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
   $\text{(i)}\iff \text{(ii)}.$ Theorem \ref{openiffsf}. 
   $\text{(i)}\implies \text{(iii)}.$ Theorem \ref{restofplweight}.
   $\text{(iii)}\implies \text{(ii)}.$ Trivial.
\end{proof}



