\section{Birational characterization of ordinary abelian varieties}

The goal of this section is to show the following particular case of \cite[Theorem 0.1]{Hacon_Patakfalvi_Zhang_Bir_char_of_AVs}:

\begin{sthm}\label{non_eff_characterization}
	A normal, proper variety $X$ is birational to an ordinary abelian variety if and only if $\kappa(X, \omega_X) = 0$, $H^0_{ss}(X, \omega_X) \neq 0$ and $b_1(X) = 2 \dim(X)$.
\end{sthm}
\begin{srem}
	\begin{itemize}
		\item The number $b_1$ is the first Betti number, i.e. the dimension of the first $l$--adic cohomology group $\dim_{\bQ_l} H^1_{\et}(X, \bQ_l)$, where $l$ denotes any prime different than $p$.
		\item Under our assumptions, the assumption $\kappa(X, \omega_X) = 0$ is equivalent to requiring that $h^0(X, \cO_X(nK_X)) = 1$ for all $n \geq 1$. 
	\end{itemize}
\end{srem}

\subsection{Preparations}

We start with a reminder on Albanese morphisms and varieties:

\begin{thm}\label{properties_Albanese}
