\section{Related Works}
\paragraph{Portfolio Optimization.}
Recent studies have highlighted the potential of machine learning methods for portfolio optimization with a limited number of equities. Gradient-based approaches to Sharpe ratio maximization have been explored \citep{Zhang_2020}, and Reinforcement Learning has frequently been applied to this problem \citep{BETANCOURT2021114002, CHAOUKI202016, Jang2023DeepRL, Jiang2024DeepRL, KORATAMADDI2021848, Yu2019ModelbasedDR, acero2024deepreinforcementlearningmeanvariance, SoodDeepRL}. In addition, \citet{lin2024a} investigated a convex formulation for Sharpe ratio maximization.

\paragraph{Decision-Focused Learning.}
Decision-Focused Learning has been analyzed and compared to Predict-then-Optimize \citep{Mandi_2024}. Recent studies have also applied Decision-Focused Learning in various domains \citep{10.1007/978-3-031-44505-7_34, NEURIPS2022_0904c7ed, kong2023df2distributionfreedecisionfocusedlearning}. \citet{lee2024anatomymachinesmarkowitzdecisionfocused} proposes a Decision-Focused Learning objective in the portfolio optimization problem. \citet{uysal2021endtoendriskbudgetingportfolio} presents a unified approach to solving the portfolio optimization problem, aligning with the principles of Decision-Focused Learning.

\paragraph{Sequence \& Time-Series Models.}
There has been extensive research on deep sequence models. Long short-term memory (LSTM) networks extend basic Recurrent Neural Networks by incorporating longer-term dependencies \citep{10.1162/neco.1997.9.8.1735}. Transformers introduce an attention mechanism that selectively extracts information over a given time horizon \citep{NIPS2017_3f5ee243}. The Mamba model offers a linear-time alternative to Transformers, reducing computational complexity relative to the sequence length \citep{gu2024mambalineartimesequencemodeling}.

\paragraph{Deep Ensemble.}
\citet{gupta2022ensembles} provided a theoretical investigation of ensembling in machine learning for classification tasks. \citet{NIPS2017_9ef2ed4b} studied the usage of Deep Ensemble on uncertainty estimation.


\section{Conclusion}
I propose a novel portfolio optimization method grounded in the Decision-Focused Learning framework. In experiments on two distinct investment universes, one trending generally upward and the other range-bound, my approach consistently outperforms various portfolio optimization baselines, indicating its robustness and superior performance across different market conditions.

To further enhance performance, I incorporate the Deep Ensemble method. My experiments show that increasing the ensemble size consistently yields better portfolio optimization results in the quality of the portfolio weight. 

\paragraph{Limitation.}
I employ a cross-entropy loss in my semi-Decision-Focused Learning framework. However, this approach is only suitable for long-only portfolios. Practitioners can extend the framework to include short positions by adopting alternative loss functions.

The effectiveness of my framework also depends on the characteristics of the target portfolio. While I examined two portfolio types, their precision is not guaranteed to be optimal, and there may exist more suitable portfolio configurations for particular investment objectives.

Although Deep Ensemble markedly improves backtesting performance, it also multiplies the computational cost. Practitioners must therefore choose an ensemble size that balances performance gains against available computational resources.

\paragraph{Future Work.}
In this study, I focus on averaging weights within a Deep Ensemble. Moving forward, I intend to develop techniques that incorporate the uncertainty from the Deep Ensemble into the final portfolio construction. Although this direction diverges from my core Semi-Decision-Focused Learning framework, it may further improve the method’s real-world applicability.

